[0.3s] # Live Art Solution
[0.3s] The crux of the bug in this problem is a misuse of functional/higher order React components.
[0.3s] Consider these lines from `src/components/drawing/index.tsx`:
[0.3s] ```tsx
[0.3s] const getWrappedError = WrapComponentError(ErrorPage)
[0.3s] const getWrappedViewer = WrapComponentError(Viewer);
[0.3s] ...
[0.3s] const _Drawing = (props: Props) => {
[0.3s]     ...
[0.3s]     const view = bigEnough
[0.3s]         ? getWrappedViewer({ image })
[0.3s]         : getWrappedError({ error: "Please make your window bigger" });
[0.3s]     return (
[0.3s]         <div>
[0.3s]             { view }
[0.3s]         </div>
[0.3s]     );
[0.3s] }
[0.3s] ```
[0.3s] This code works, since the components are just functions, and the result of using a higher order component is still just a functional component. However, the difference is that the children components are being processed **in the same fiber** as the parent component.
[0.3s] Why is this a problem? It means that React hooks used by the children components will be bound to the parent component.
[0.3s] Let's look a bit closer at those two children:
[0.3s] ### `src/components/error/index.tsx`
[0.3s] ```tsx
[0.3s] export const ErrorPage = (props: Props) => {
[0.3s]     const params = useHashParams<{ error: string, returnTo: string }>();
[0.3s]     const error = props.error ?? params.error;
[0.3s]     const returnTo = props.returnTo ?? params.returnTo;
[0.3s]     return (
[0.3s]         <div>
[0.3s]             <h1>Uh Oh Spaghetti-Oh!</h1>
[0.3s]             <h3>{ error }</h3>
[0.3s]             <div>
[0.3s]                 <a href={ returnTo }>Return to previous page</a> or <a href="/">go home</a>.
[0.3s]             </div>
[0.3s]         </div>
[0.3s]     )
[0.3s] }
[0.3s] ```
[0.3s] The error page uses a single hook, called `useHashParams`. However, this hook in turn is defined as (`/src/hooks/index.tsx`):
[0.3s] ```tsx
[0.3s] export const useHashParams = <T extends Record<string, string>>() => {
[0.3s]     const [params, setParams] = React.useState(getHashParams<T>());
[0.3s]     React.useEffect(() => {
[0.3s]         const listener = () => {
[0.3s]             setParams(getHashParams<T>());
[0.3s]         }
[0.3s]         window.addEventListener("hashchange", listener);
[0.3s]         return () => {
[0.3s]             window.removeEventListener("hashchange", listener);
[0.3s]         }
[0.3s]     });
[0.3s]     return params;
[0.3s] };
[0.3s] ```
[0.3s] Notice that it uses both a `useState` and a `useEffect` hook. Since nested hooks ultimately get attached to the component the invoked the top-level hook, these are both now attached to the error page, which from the above means it's actually bound to the `_Drawing` component.
[0.3s] ### `src/components/viewer/index.tsx`
[0.3s] ```tsx
[0.3s] export const Viewer = (props: Props) => {
[0.3s]     const [dimensions, updateDimensions] = React.useReducer(
[0.3s]         (canvasDimensions: Dimensions, windowDimensions: Dimensions) => {
[0.3s]             const newScale = Math.floor(Math.min(
[0.3s]                 (windowDimensions.width / baseResolution.width),
[0.3s]                 (windowDimensions.height / baseResolution.height))
[0.3s]             );
[0.3s]             const desiredDimensions = { width: baseResolution.width * newScale, height: baseResolution.height * newScale };
[0.3s]             if (desiredDimensions.width !== canvasDimensions.width || desiredDimensions.height !== canvasDimensions.height) {
[0.3s]                 return desiredDimensions;
[0.3s]             } else {
[0.3s]                 return canvasDimensions;
[0.3s]             }
[0.3s]         },
[0.3s]         baseResolution
[0.3s]     );
[0.3s]     React.useEffect(() => {
[0.3s]         const listener = () => {
[0.3s]             updateDimensions({ width: window.innerWidth - 100, height: window.innerHeight - 200 });
[0.3s]         }
[0.3s]         window.addEventListener("resize", listener);
[0.3s]         return () => {
[0.3s]             window.removeEventListener("resize", listener);
[0.3s]         }
[0.3s]     }, []);
[0.3s]     return (
[0.3s]         <div>
[0.3s]             <h1>Viewing</h1>
